{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 7, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind in Wonderland: My Brief Trip to Japan**\n\nTokyo’s skyline at dusk never fails to dazzle—neon lights reflecting off rain-slick streets, a symphony of honking taxis and the faint scent of green tea in the air. I started my journey in **Shinjuku**, where the energy was electric. Towering skyscrapers stood beside tiny izakayas, and the Omoide Yokocho alleyways hummed with laughter and clinking sake cups. A quick detour to **Meiji Shrine** offered quiet contrast, its towering torii gate marking the entrance to a serene forest.\n\nNext stop: **Kyoto**, where tradition breathed life into every corner. Wandering through **Fushimi Inari’s** thousands of red torii gates felt like stepping into a dream. The early morning mist over **Kinkaku-ji’s** golden pavilion was surreal—still and shimmering. At **Arashiyama**, bamboo groves swayed gently, and the river’s gentle flow lulled my tired feet. A chance encounter with a tea master led to a quiet ceremony in a tiny garden, where matcha’s earthy sweetness lingered long after.\n\nThe final chapter was **Osaka**, where food reigned supreme. **Dotonbori’s** vibrant signs and sizzling takoyaki stalls tempted me at every turn. Slurping bowls of ramen at a 24-hour shop with a local salaryman became an unforgettable night. Before the flight home, a last-minute visit to **Universal Studios Japan** delivered thrills—Super Nintendo World’s bright blue and red walls made even the jet-lagged heart smile.\n\nJapan’s magic lies in its contrasts: ancient and modern, chaotic and calm, humble and extravagant. Even a short trip left me craving more—one steaming bowl, one temple step, one neon-lit street at a time.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.07108993083238602}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.32481810450553894}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.0516633577644825}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.014